# 🩺 CKD Prediction Web App | Machine Learning + Flask

## 📊 1. Project Overview

The **CKD Prediction Web App** is a Machine Learning-based web application developed to predict whether a patient is likely to have **Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD)** based on selected clinical parameters.

The project combines **Machine Learning, Python, Flask, SQL database management, and HTML/CSS** to provide an interactive web-based prediction system.

The application allows users to:

- Create an account and log in securely
- Enter patient clinical information
- Generate a CKD prediction using a trained Machine Learning model
- Store patient information in a database
- View previously entered patient records
- Generate patient reports in PDF format
- Manage application settings

The main objective of this project is to demonstrate how a Machine Learning model can be integrated into a real-world web application.

![CKD Prediction Web App](screenshots/home.png)


## 🧩 2. Problem Statement

Chronic Kidney Disease is a condition that can affect kidney function over time. Identifying possible CKD cases using clinical information can help demonstrate how data-driven systems can support healthcare-related analysis.

Traditional analysis of multiple clinical parameters can require manual evaluation. A Machine Learning model can process several input parameters together and generate a prediction.

This project focuses on building a web-based system where users can enter clinical information and obtain a Machine Learning-based CKD prediction.


## 🎯 3. Objectives

The main objectives of this project are:

- To develop a Machine Learning model for CKD prediction.
- To use clinical parameters as input features.
- To preprocess and prepare the dataset for Machine Learning.
- To save the trained model using Joblib.
- To integrate the Machine Learning model with Flask.
- To create an easy-to-use web interface.
- To store patient information using a database.
- To provide patient records through the web application.
- To generate patient reports in PDF format.
- To demonstrate an end-to-end Machine Learning application.


## 🛠️ 4. Technologies Used

| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Python | Programming and Machine Learning |
| Pandas | Data processing |
| Scikit-learn | Machine Learning |
| Joblib | Saving and loading the trained model |
| Flask | Web application development |
| Flask-SQLAlchemy | Database integration |
| Flask-Migrate | Database migration |
| Flask-Mail | Email functionality |
| HTML | Web page structure |
| CSS | Web page styling |
| JavaScript | Front-end functionality |
| SQLite | Application database |
| GitHub | Project version control |


